{
  "probe": "e0b-pad-snap",
  "question": "In the PRODUCTION pixel-format chain (PNG -> yuva420p -> overlay on yuv420p), where does the contained picture actually land — and is the gray-format E0-b table still the right one to hold the preview to?",
  "answer": "No. With chroma subsampling the scaled size floors to the even grid (1920x1080 into a 634x356 box measures 632 wide, not the 633 gray reported) and so does the centring offset — but the offset is computed from the size BEFORE that snap, then floored: a raw 21.5 offset lands at 20, not at the 22 you get by centring the snapped size. The preview has to replay THIS table, because it is the one the shipped file is rendered with.",
  "label": "dev",
  "ffmpeg": "ffmpeg",
